            <div xml:id="d635">

                <pb facs="0647" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815B.20/82: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General in Martinique (Malige) to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort-de-France</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-13T10:00:00-04:00">July 13, 1942—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>263. From Reber. My 260, July 10.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d635-f1"/> Robert has been
                    informed by his Government that the agreement giving United States Consul at
                    Casablanca permanent control of the parts taken from the ships <pb facs="0648"
                        n="642" xml:id="pg642"/> and planes here will be carried out and that new
                    instructions have been sent to Casablanca so that there will be no further
                    misunderstanding. [Reber.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Malige</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
